                <pb facs="0787" n="711" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg711"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5231/977: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-01T13:00:00+00:00">June 1, 1935—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 1—10:47 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. My telegram No. 37, May 28, 11 a.m. Italian Chargé d’Affaires said yesterday
                    Spanish Foreign Office apparently in attempt to hurry Italian-Spanish commercial
                    negotiations has informed him it was expected that Spanish-American treaty would
                    be signed from one day to another. Gather that Spaniards are trying to play off
                    one country with which they were negotiating against another.</p>
                <p>Spanish exporters have been pressing Government for American treaty and believe
                    Government now realizes more fully desirability of signing treaty with us before
                    October. Spanish commercial relations with England easier since cold weather in
                    England compelling additional purchase fresh vegetables et cetera in Spain.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
